          "text": "<S0>Let's think step by step:</S0>\n\n1. The Response mentions that either party may end the agreement for material breach that is not remedied within 30 days of written notice.\n2. The Ground Truth also mentions that the contract runs from July 1, 2024 to June 30, 2027 and renews for one year unless either party gives notice 90 days before it ends.\n3. However, the Response does not mention the renewal clause or the notice period for renewal.\n4. The Response does mention that Fabrikam Seals delivers within six weeks of an order and reports any quality incident that affects delivered parts within five business days, which is not relevant to the contract terms.\n5. The Response does not contain any information that is not present in the Ground Truth, but it also does not contain any additional information that is relevant to the contract terms.\n\n<S1>Based on the definitions, I think the Response should get a Score of 3 because it contains most of the necessary and relevant information with respect to the Ground Truth, but it misses some minor information, such as the renewal clause and the notice period for renewal.</S1>\n\n<S2>3</S2>"
